+
+# JSON Pointer: export JsonPointerError and parsePointer for later features
+
+## Context
+
+The request says the next features build on JSON Pointer. Features such as JSON Patch (RFC 6902) need
+to walk a pointer down to the parent of the target and then act on the last token, and need to tell
+pointer errors apart from other errors.
+
+## Decision
+
+`src/index.ts` exports, besides `resolvePointer`:
+
+- `parsePointer(pointer): string[]`, which validates a pointer and returns its decoded reference tokens;
+- `JsonPointerError`, an `Error` subclass carrying the offending `pointer`, thrown for every invalid
+  or unresolvable pointer.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Later features reuse one parser and one escape-decoding rule instead of duplicating them.
+- Callers can `catch` with `instanceof JsonPointerError`; the error class and `parsePointer` are now part
+  of the public API and must stay stable.
