+# Implement RFC 6901 JSON Pointer resolvePointer
+
+## Request
+
+Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`: return the value a JSON Pointer
+(RFC 6901) refers to, throw when the pointer is invalid or does not resolve.
+
+## Done
+
+- `src/index.ts`: `resolvePointer`, `parsePointer` and `JsonPointerError`, with no runtime dependency.
+- `test/resolve-pointer.test.ts` (run with `npm test`, Node.js 22.18+ type stripping), written first
+  and seen failing: all examples of RFC 6901 section 5, `~01` decoding order, falsy values, primitive
+  roots, object members named like indices, invalid syntax, non-string pointer, missing members,
+  inherited properties, malformed/out-of-range/`-` indices, descending into primitives.
+- `README.md`: usage and error behaviour.
+- Decisions: dl-001 (strict resolution semantics), dl-002 (exported error class and parser).
+
+## Notes
+
+- TypeScript is not installed in the repository, so `tsc` type-checking was not run; the tests run the
+  source through Node's type stripping.
